-- title:
--   Maximum principle on a node tube: integrality at the node places
-- statement:
--   Let $q\ge 5$ be a prime and $M'$ a nonzero natural number with $q\nmid M'$. Let $A$ be a valuation subring of $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ in which $q$ is a nonunit, let $k_0$ be an intermediate field of $\overline{\mathbb Q}/\mathbb Q$, let $\pi_0\in k_0$ have image in $A$, and put $A_0=A\cap k_0$ (the comap of $A$ along $k_0\to\overline{\mathbb Q}$); assume $A_0$ is a henselian discrete valuation ring with $\mathfrak m_{A_0}=(\pi_0)$ and algebraically closed residue field, and that every $a\in A$ differs from some element of $k_0\cap A$ by an element of $\mathfrak m_A$. Write $F=\,$`fieldBar q M'`$\,=\,$`xHFunctionFieldBar`$(q^2M',\,$`levelH`$\,q\,M')$, a $k_0$-algebra through $\overline{\mathbb Q}$. The assertion is made for every intermediate field $F_0$ of $F/k_0$ with $\overline{\mathbb Q}\cdot F_0=F$ and satisfying the stated disjointness condition (for $K'/k_0$ finite inside $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, any family from $\overline{\mathbb Q}$ linearly independent over $K'$ stays independent over $\overline{\mathbb Q}K'\cdot F_0$); every valuation subring $W_0$ of $F_0$ that is a discrete valuation ring, traces $A$ on $k_0$ and has $\mathfrak m_{W_0}$ generated by $\pi_0$; every local Noetherian subring $O\subseteq W_0$ of $F_0$ tracing $A$ on $k_0$, whose every element is congruent to an element of $k_0\cap A\cap O$ modulo nonunits, and with $F_0$ the ring of fractions of $O$; every $E_0\ge 1$, $c_x,c_y\in O$, $u\in O^\times$ with $c_xc_y=\pi_0^{E_0}u$, and every ring isomorphism $\iota$ from the $\mathfrak m_O$-adic completion of $O$ onto the crossing model $\mathrm{MvPowerSeries}(\mathrm{Fin}\,2,\widehat{A_0})/\,$`uvCrossingIdeal` at $\hat\pi_0^{E_0}$, $\widehat{A_0}$ the $\mathfrak m_{A_0}$-adic completion, such that $\iota$ sends each element of $k_0\cap A\cap O$ to the corresponding constant series and $\iota(c_x)=\gamma_U\cdot U$, $\iota(c_y)=\gamma_V\cdot V$ for units $\gamma_U,\gamma_V$; with $c_y\in\mathfrak m_{W_0}$ and $c_x\notin\mathfrak m_{W_0}$; every valuation subring $W_x\supseteq O$ of $F_0$ that is a discrete valuation ring tracing $A$ on $k_0$, with $\mathfrak m_{W_x}$ generated by $\pi_0$, $c_x\in\mathfrak m_{W_x}$ and $c_y\notin\mathfrak m_{W_x}$; and every pair of regular prolongations $R$, $R_x$ of $A$ to $F$ (with residue fields $FSS$, $FI$ over the residue field of $A$) whose rings of integers meet $F_0$ in $W_0$, respectively $W_x$. Finally let $S$ be the set of places $P$ of $F/\overline{\mathbb Q}$ — valuation subrings of $F$ containing $\overline{\mathbb Q}$, proper, with principal ideals — such that every element of $O$ is $P$-integral and, for every nonunit $f$ of $O$, $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)$ lies in $\mathfrak m_A$. Then for every $f\in F$ lying in the integers of $R_x$, in the integers of $R$, and in $P$ for all $P\in S$, one has $P.\mathrm{evalAt}(f)\in A$ for every $P\in S$, where $P.\mathrm{evalAt}$ denotes the $\overline{\mathbb Q}$-valued evaluation obtained from the residue map of $P$.
--
--   This is the non-archimedean maximum principle for the tube around a node of the semistable reduction: through the crossing presentation the places in $S$ form the open annulus $|\pi_0|^{E_0}<|U|<1$ and the two regular prolongations $R$, $R_x$ are the Gauss valuations of its boundary circles, so integrality on both ends plus regularity inside forces integral values throughout. It supplies the integrality hypothesis needed by the node-annulus machinery and is used in the construction of node centres and node charts for the full-level modular curve.
